wh40k-company-kasballica-name = Kasballica
wh40k-company-kasballica-description =
    The Kasballica Mission represents the crime barons of the Drusus Marches in the Calixis Sector on Footfall. Its brokers purchase finds from the Koronus Expanse, arrange discreet shipping and engage in the Cold Trade: the illegal traffic in xenos artefacts and technology.

    Discretion, useful contacts and keeping agreements matter here. Mission associates escort cargo, guard warehouses and find buyers. Kasballica connections offer no protection from Imperial law.

    On Footfall, Oliva Krakovskaya represents the Mission; Leman Londoron trades in weapons and equipment.
wh40k-company-fleet-name = Fleet
wh40k-company-fleet-description =
    The Chartist Merchant Fleet carries cargo and supplies Imperial worlds. Its captains operate under merchant charters defining their rights and routes. Chartist vessels belong to the merchant branch of the Imperial Fleet; the battle squadrons of the Imperial Navy serve a different purpose.

    On Footfall, the trading mission supplies transports, records cargo and guards warehouses. Voidsmen serve aboard ships for generations. Associates are expected to observe discipline, honour their charter and care for their ship and cargo.

    The local representative is Officer Severin Holt. Ship's quartermaster Livia Dorn sells uniforms, provisions and equipment.
